--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This file carries the license notices for code that Farhelm ported from
xterm.js and from Visual Studio Code into its own grid terminal and its
supervisor's input encoder. The ports are Farhelm source, not vendored
copies, so this notice stands on its own; xterm.js itself no longer
ships with Farhelm.

The code was ported from @xterm/xterm 6.0.0, its @xterm/addon-fit 0.11.0
and @xterm/addon-web-links 0.12.0 add-ons, and the part of Visual Studio
Code's vs/base that xterm.js 6.0.0 compiles in (shipped in @xterm/xterm's
src/vs/). Where it lives:

- crates/farhelm-ui/assets/grid-input.js: the keydown decision
  (evaluateKeyboardEvent and its KEYCODE_KEY_MAPPINGS from
  src/common/input/Keyboard.ts; the filters of CoreBrowserTerminal's
  _keyDown and _isThirdLevelShift; the Mac platform list of
  src/common/Platform.ts), mouse cell rounding (getCoords,
  src/browser/input/Mouse.ts), mouse move de-duplication and wheel step
  accumulation (CoreMouseService's _equalEvents and consumeWheelEvent), and
  the Alt-click cursor move (src/browser/input/MoveToCell.ts).
- crates/farhelm-ui/assets/grid-terminal.js: character measurement
  (CharSizeService), cell size (DomRenderer's _updateDimensions), the fit
  (@xterm/addon-fit's proposeDimensions), selection coordinates, drag
  scrolling and column selection (SelectionService), placing the input
  field under the pointer (moveTextAreaUnderMouseCursor,
  src/browser/Clipboard.ts), and the wheel's scroll distance (Visual Studio
  Code's StandardWheelEvent and ScrollableElement's _onMouseWheel).
- crates/farhelm-ui/assets/grid-buffer.js: selection text and word
  selection (SelectionService), the default word separators, and the URL
  pattern, its line window and its URL check (@xterm/addon-web-links).
- crates/farhelm-supervisor/src/grid_input.rs, compiled into the farhelm
  binary: key encoding (evaluateKeyboardEvent), mouse report encoding
  (CoreMouseService, and CoreBrowserTerminal's wheel on the alternate
  screen), and paste line endings (prepareTextForTerminal,
  src/browser/Clipboard.ts).

This notice ships inside the distributed bundles: GRID_PORTED_CODE_LICENSES
in ../src/lib.rs declares this file as an asset, so the web bundle, the
desktop app and every release farhelm binary (which embeds the web bundle)
carry it. THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md at the repository root says the same for
the source tree.

The xterm.js text is copied verbatim from the LICENSE file of @xterm/xterm
6.0.0 as published to npm; the add-ons' texts from their own LICENSE files;
the Visual Studio Code text from LICENSE.txt at the root of
https://github.com/microsoft/vscode, which the vs/base sources cite.

